; outbreak.ini: start-up settings of the runner (PS2Recomp patch 0043). Copy as outbreak.ini beside
; ps2EntryRunner.exe (Windows), or into the app's files dir on Android
; (/sdcard/Android/data/com.outbreakmodern.app/files/outbreak.ini). PS2X_SETTINGS=<path> names another file.
; Read once at start-up. One "key = value" per line; a line starting with ';' or '#' is a comment (so a path
; may contain both). Keys are case-insensitive. A value may be in double quotes. A relative path is relative
; to this file's folder. A bad line is logged once as "[settings] line N: ..." and ignored; the runner logs
; "[settings] from <path> (N bad line(s)): game=... textures=... mods=... saves=... upscale=... window=...".

; game: your copy of the game. One of
;   - the disc image (ISO 9660, .iso), read in place: nothing is extracted or loaded whole;
;   - a folder with the disc's files copied out (the boot file comes from its SYSTEM.CNF);
;   - the boot ELF inside such a folder (SLPM_654.28), as before.
; A path on the command line wins over this. Android: when game is not set, the one .iso in the app's files
; dir is used.
game = D:\Games\PS2\Biohazard - Outbreak (English v2.1).iso

; textures: optional root of texture packs in PCSX2's layout, <root>\<serial>\replacements
; (here <root>\SLPM-65428\replacements, .png/.dds in any subfolders), or a <root>\SLPM-65428.zip. Loaded by
; PCSX2's texture replacement with the Vulkan renderer (PS2X_GS=pcsx2-vk on Windows; always on Android, where
; a relative root such as "textures = textures" is the app's files folder).
; The start-up log line "[pcsx2-gs] open ... replacements=found" confirms the pack was seen.
; textures = D:\Games\PS2\textures

; saves: the folder that holds your memory cards (patch 0072), PCSX2's own .ps2 card files: Mcd001.ps2 is the
; card in slot 1, Mcd002.ps2 (only if you put one there) the card in slot 2. The same files PCSX2 keeps in its
; memcards folder, so a card can be copied between PCSX2 and the runner either way (8 MB cards; close PCSX2 first:
; a card in use by one cannot be opened by the other). A missing Mcd001.ps2 is created blank; the game then
; offers to format it, as with a new card on a PS2. Saves reach the file as soon as the game writes them.
; Default: a "memcards" folder beside ps2EntryRunner.exe (Windows), or in the app's files dir on Android
; (/sdcard/Android/data/com.outbreakmodern.app/files/memcards). The log shows the folder used:
; "[sio2] pcsx2 memory cards in <folder> (settings|default)". PS2X_SAVES=<folder> wins over this.
; saves = D:\Games\PS2\saves

; mods: optional root for mods. Today: PCSX2 .pnach patch files in <root>\<serial>\ (here
; <root>\SLPM-65428\*.pnach), memory writes only (patch 0050). Code patches are skipped with a log line: the
; game's code is compiled ahead of time. Widescreen: a file with these lines (the gameplay part of
; SLPM-65428_32088394.pnach in PCSX2's resources\patches.zip, "gameplay by synce"):
;   gsaspectratio=16:9
;   patch=1,EE,20239d48,extended,3fe38e38
; mods = D:\Games\PS2\mods

; upscale: render resolution multiplier, 1 (native) to 8. Vulkan renderer only (PS2X_GS=pcsx2-vk); 3 is about
; 1080p. Default: 3 on Android, 1 on Windows. Make the window bigger to see the detail (window below, or resize it).
; upscale = 3

; scaling: how the finished picture is stretched to the window: smooth (bilinear) or sharp (nearest, hard pixel
; edges). Default: smooth on Android, sharp on Windows.
; scaling = smooth

; window: the window's size at start-up, <width>x<height> (at least 320x224). Default: 640x448, or 797x448 with a
; 16:9 pnach. The window can be resized while playing.
; window = 1440x810

; gpu_driver: Android only. The Vulkan driver the game draws with: system (the phone's own, the default) or the
; name of a driver folder you put in the app's files dir as drivers/<name>/ (meta.json + the driver .so, e.g. a
; Mesa Turnip package for Adreno). If that driver cannot be used, the log says why and the system driver is used.
; Ignored on Windows. Steps: docs/ops/android.md "GPU driver".
; gpu_driver = system

; gs_self_read: how the Vulkan renderer reads back what it has just drawn when a draw blends with it (light glows,
; menu backgrounds). auto (the default) = through a copy of the picture on Qualcomm's own Adreno driver, whose fast
; read returns stale colour (black glows), PCSX2's own choice everywhere else. copy / barrier / fetch force one way,
; for testing a phone or driver. The log shows the choice: [gpu] self-read=... Steps: docs/ops/android.md.
; gs_self_read = auto

; vu1: the PS2's second vector unit (it transforms the 3D geometry). mvu = a recompiler (fast: Windows PCSX2's
; microVU, Android ARMSX2's ARM64 microVU), interp = the interpreter (slow, the reference). Default: interp on
; Windows, mvu on Android. The PS2X_VU1 environment variable wins over this. If mvu cannot load or start, the log
; says why and the interpreter runs.
; vu1 = mvu
